text:
rachel: Quick heads-up 1 opened PR #8124 to add a short section on tiered pricing examples and to correct two stale dashboard links on the Quotas & Billing page. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/8124

omar: Thanks. Can you call out which exact panels changed? I want to make sure the product pages link to the canonical view.

rachel: Sure  replaced old panel /d/old/usage with /d/new/usage-slab and swapped /d/old/billing with /d/new/billing-slab. docs-bot flagged them in CI as 404s. I also added an example query that shows how to compute monthly spend for a given customer_id across tiers.

docs-bot: Automated check: broken links detected in PR -> https://grafana.redwood.ai/d/old/usage, https://grafana.redwood.ai/d/old/billing returned 404. Suggested replacements provided in PR comment.

billing: Quick review note  when adding the pricing example, please make it explicit that credits and applied discounts are applied after tier aggregation (i.e., invoice math: subtotal by tier -> discounts -> credits -> invoice total). Left suggested copy in PR.

jin: For the docs example, can we show a compact PromQL snippet that teams can paste into Grafana to compute "tiered_tokens" across a billing window? I proposed this in the PR: `sum(rate(tokens_total[1m])) by (customer_id, tier)` with a downstream `topk` to show top customers.

omar: Nice. Also request an SDK snippet (JS) that demonstrates reading a quota header and the new "usage_slab" header we recently added. Prefer to show resilient parsing and a small comment about units.

rachel: Added a JS snippet in the PR. Pasting the snippet here so reviewers can see it quickly:

```javascript
// JS SDK: parse quota headers and normalize units
function parseHeader(headers, nameCandidates) {
  for (const n of nameCandidates) {
    const v = headers[n];
    if (v) return v;
  }
  return null;
}

const header = parseHeader(response.headers, ['x-rw-usage-slab', 'x-usage-slab', 'x-quota-tier']);
if (header) {
  // header examples: "gold: 5000/min", "silver: 1000"
  const parts = header.split(':');
  const tier = parts.length > 1 ? parts[0].trim() : 'unknown';
  const qty = parseInt((parts[1] || '').replace(/[^0-9]/g, ''), 10);
  // normalize missing unit to per-minute in our examples
}
```

billing: Also please add one sentence clarifying that tier thresholds are evaluated at the customer_id rollup and invoices may show aggregated usage differently than per-key dashboards. This avoids the recent support confusion where teams thought keys were independent billing units.

rachel: Added the sentence and a short example SQL/flux-like pseudocode demonstrating grouping by customer_id: `SELECT sum(tokens) FROM usage WHERE ts >= $start GROUP BY customer_id, tier`

jin: Minor nit  the migration guide should show how to update alerts that used the old single-tier metric to the new slab-aware metric, and include the Grafana panel ID so users can update their dashboards easily. I've added that in a small migration subsection.

docs-bot: Style/lint: codeblock in the PR uses backticks but missing language tag, suggested adding ` ```javascript ` for clarity. Also confirm the replacement Grafana links respond (I will recheck after the commit).

omar: One more ask: can we include a short paragraph about how burst credits are consumed when a customer spans multiple tiers in the same month? i.e., credits are consumed after tier math, and pro-rated as needed. That should reduce support confusion.

billing: Agreed. I left suggested wording in the PR: "Burst credits are applied at the customer_id level after tier calculations; if a customer moves tiers mid-cycle credits are pro-rated across the billing window."

rachel: Included both the migration note and the burst-credit paragraph. Also updated the PR to point at the new Grafana panels: https://grafana.redwood.ai/d/new/usage-slab and https://grafana.redwood.ai/d/new/billing-slab (commit a12d4).

devrel: LGTM  small but helpful. Suggest adding a one-line example in the changelog blurb: "Docs: clarified tier billing math and updated Grafana links (usage-slab, billing-slab)."

jin: I'll proof the PromQL snippet and add an example of a 30-day rollup for the billing window.

rachel: Plan: final docs proofread this afternoon, wait for docs-bot link re-check and jin's minor edits, then merge. Will add the changelog under "Pricing & Quotas" for the next minor. Ping me if you want me to split the PR into two (docs vs links) but I kept it together for easier testing.

omar: Thanks all. Please ping once merged so I can update partner-facing KBs.

rachel: Will do 1 merging after checks pass. Thanks!
